// Q-076 `/_quillo/health` is the process's own: the app answers 200 with the service it calls down, there is no readiness of what it calls, and a gateway cannot reach a service's health through it
// mode: serve
// flags: --service-url risk=http://127.0.0.1:9
// get: /_quillo/health
// get: /_quillo/ready
// get: /go
// open-when: GET /_quillo/ready -> 404
// fixed-when: GET /_quillo/ready -> 503
// From FEEDBACK10.md §Q-076 (found on af64ac8). risk "runs" at port 9, where nothing answers. `/_quillo/ready` is the suggestion's name.

service risk = "risk.qwe" { timeout: "1s", retries: 0 }

route GET /go = risk.assess(1) ?? "risk did not answer"
